---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="The maths · Wörgl" description="A calculator, a chart and the proof: how a Wörgl balance is worked out." active="/maths">
<!-- THE MATHS -->
<section class="section lead-section" aria-labelledby="maths-title">
  <h1 id="maths-title" class="page-title">The maths</h1>
  <p class="prose">The rule is short: every balance loses 1% on a fixed schedule, and the loss goes to the pot. Three levels follow, from a calculator to the proof.</p>

  <h2 style="margin-top:var(--s7)">Try a number</h2>
  <p class="prose">At the real setting, 1% every month.</p>
  <form class="calc" id="calc" novalidate>
    <div class="row">
      <div><label for="calc-coins">Coins</label><input id="calc-coins" value="100" inputmode="decimal" size="10"></div>
      <div><label for="calc-time">Time</label><input id="calc-time" value="6" inputmode="decimal" size="6"></div>
      <div><label for="calc-unit">Unit</label><select id="calc-unit"><option value="d">days</option><option value="m" selected>months</option><option value="y">years</option></select></div>
    </div>
    <p id="calc-out" class="readout" role="status"></p>
  </form>
  <table class="shelf" id="shelf"><caption class="sr-only">A 100-coin note over time at the real melt rate</caption></table>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="sim-title">
  <h2 id="sim-title">A 60-day simulation</h2>
  <figure class="chart" id="chart">
    <img id="chart-fallback" hidden src="/assets/simulation.png" alt="Chart of a 60-day simulation with 100 wallets: the pot falls as the DAO pays coins out, while some coins melt back; an idle holder's 100 coins fall to about 55 while a wallet paid by the pot keeps its balance up." width="1650" height="880">
    <figcaption>Illustrative: this simulation melts 1% per day so 60 days show the shape. It has 100 wallets that each claim 100 coins on day 0. The top chart is the same in all three runs, because trading cannot avoid the melt.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="proof-title">
  <h2 id="proof-title" class="sr-only">The proof</h2>
  <details class="proof">
    <summary>For people who check: shares and the index</summary>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Nothing on the chain changes every second. The contract stores your <b>shares</b>. One <b>index</b> falls with time, and your balance is worked out when somebody reads it.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="formula num">balance = floor(shares × index ÷ 10<sup>27</sup>)</p>
    <div class="check-controls">
      <label for="who-input">Whose numbers</label>
      <div class="row"><input id="who-input" placeholder="an account, such as friend.testnet" size="32" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off"><button id="who-go" type="button">Look up</button><button id="who-all" type="button">Everyone together</button></div>
    </div>
    <dl class="ledger check" id="check" aria-live="off"></dl>
    <p class="faded" id="check-note"></p>
    <p>Balances round down and the total in circulation rounds up, so rounding always favours the pot. Checks in the repository: <a id="link-tests" href="#">the unit tests</a>, <a id="link-math" href="#">the maths module</a>, and two 100,000-step fuzz tests that check the supply is conserved. <code>scripts/verify-testnet.sh</code> re-derives these numbers from raw chain state.</p>
  </details>
</section>
<p class="next">Questions people ask? <a class="button solid" href="/faq">Next: questions and limits</a></p>
</Base>
